/* Life in Harem */ Correction of the article, 

She never ordered killing of her spouse Al-Mutawakkil but it was [[al-Musta'in]] (nephew of Al-Mutawakkil).

This article was repeating the same claim twice, that's why I corrected it.

/* Twelver View */ This is a Shia view and historical view.

Historically pre Islamic Arabs were absolute monotheists or monotheists with belief in multiple subordinate Gods like Hubal, Allat, Manat, Uzza, etc 
Some Arabs were secular and minority were Christian or Jewish converts, (two minority Abrahamic religions).

/* Ruling elites and Government */ Improvement :
 Al-Ya'qubi 1892, pp. 264–65.
 Northedge 2008, pp. 225–27

/* */ Question mark removed!!
If the mother is not known at all.
Leave the section blank.

